data 441
Article 116: Time to file a civil action
A victim of an offence may file a civil action to a competent court in order to be indemnified, from the time when the court is seized with the criminal action to the time when the proceedings are closed at first instance. The court informs the concerned parties thereof.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

