mark :382
original-oid 66caf76c4acebe4f49690da0f51fbec0adfb4f39
data 447
Article 117: Withdrawal of a civil action within criminal proceedings
A person aggrieved by an offence who files a civil action within criminal proceedings may withdraw the action at any time until the closing of the proceedings. He or she may do so by giving notice before the hearing or in the course of the hearing.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

blob
mark :383
original-oid 47d3fc686508a3f2ada7a7549315643a63a92a56
data 492
Article 118: Private prosecution
A victim of an offence may initiate criminal proceedings by way of private prosecution.
Private prosecution is carried out when the victim of an offence files a claim in a criminal court demanding that the offender, his or her co- offender or accomplice be punished and be ordered to pay damages proportional to the injury caused.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

blob
mark :384
original-oid beb3c53dc7128da778e65856279f3146827388a4
data 546
Article 119: Identification of acts the accused is alleged to have committed
A person who files an action by way of private prosecution must clearly indicate acts the defendant is accused to have committed to enable him or her to properly prepare his or her case expeditiously.
Aggravating circumstances, if any, must also be indicated in the complaint to enable the accused to present his or her defence accordingly.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

blob
mark :385
original-oid f46312b4adcbb57065f4daacfeaa6e2e143a53cd
data 849
Article 120: Filing a claim by way of private prosecution
Filing a claim by way of private prosecution takes place when a criminal case file is finally closed without further action or when a period of three (3) months for petty offences and six (6) months for misdemeanours and felonies elapse after the public prosecution receives the file but without taking any action.
The time limits provided for under Paragraph One of this Article are counted from the time the case is referred to the prosecution or from the time a criminal case file is forwarded to the public prosecution from the organ in charge of investigation. The court seized notifies the public prosecution with an obligation to get involved in the case.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

blob
mark :386
original-oid 0edf4162288308e7a38a2f0d1adb2929de16216f
data 792
Article 121: Discontinuance of a claim submitted by way of private prosecution
A victim of an offence who filed a case in a court by way of private prosecution may at any time, discontinue a claim from the time of filing the case to the time of closure of the proceedings by doing it in the court proceedings or in the registry of the court seized. If discontinuance of a claim is done in the court registry, the court registrar has the obligation to notify the concerned parties.
However, withdrawing the civil action when the victim of the offence filed the case with the court by way of private prosecution does not prevent continuation of the criminal action.
Chapter: CHAPTER ONE: PROSECUTION OF THE ACCUSED AT THE FIRST INSTANCE
Section: Section 4: Civil action arising from an offence

