Article 226: Grounds for suspension of the execution of penalty
The grounds for suspension of the execution of the penalty are the following:
1° presidential pardon;
2° release on parole;
3° suspension of the penalty.
Chapter: CHAPTER II: GROUNDS FOR SUSPENSION OF THE EXECUTION OF A PENALTY AND REMOVAL OF A PENALTY
Section: Section One: Grounds for suspension of the execution of penalty

blob
mark :492
original-oid 1d982b8cfc36d2d398d29fddf83957716433e766
data 718
Article 227: Prerogative of pardon of the President of the Republic
The President of the Republic has the prerogative of mercy for a convict sentenced by a final judgment, upon application or by his or her own initiative, and after consultation with the Supreme Court.
Presidential pardon is granted by the President of the Republic under his or her sole discretion and for public interest.
Presidential pardon remits in whole or in part penalties imposed or commute them to less severe penalties.
Chapter: CHAPTER II: GROUNDS FOR SUSPENSION OF THE EXECUTION OF A PENALTY AND REMOVAL OF A PENALTY
Section: Section One: Grounds for suspension of the execution of penalty
Subsection: Subsection One: Presidential pardon

blob
mark :493
original-oid 1ea862451298e8d365a6861977006303c6312847
data 1395
Article 228: Presidential pardon on application by a convicted person
Application for presidential pardon is lodged by a convict or his or her representative following the procedure set by the law. The applicant for presidential pardon indicates reasons for such application.
Application for presidential pardon is made in writing and addressed to the President of the Republic through the administration in charge of correctional services if the applicant is in prison, with a copy to the Minister in charge of justice.
Upon reception of the application for presidential pardon by the Commissioner General of Rwanda Correctional Service, he or she immediately makes a report accompanying the application indicating the following:
1° identification of the applicant or of the person for whom presidential pardon is applied;
2° offence for which he or she was imprisoned;
3° the decision of the court at the last instance that sentenced him or her;
4° the period completed in serving the sentence and the remaining period;
5° his or her conduct in the prison with supporting evidence;
6° advice of Rwanda Correctional Service on the application for presidential pardon.
Chapter: CHAPTER II: GROUNDS FOR SUSPENSION OF THE EXECUTION OF A PENALTY AND REMOVAL OF A PENALTY
Section: Section One: Grounds for suspension of the execution of penalty
Subsection: Subsection One: Presidential pardon

blob
mark :494
original-oid 78f702a9adbddd1a887ffea88ea4688b2bc1a8cb
data 1070
Article 229: Collective pardon granted by the President of the Republic
Collective pardon granted by the President of the Republic is requested by the Minister in charge of justice after presenting justifications.
The request of the Minister in charge of justice must be accompanied by a report of the Commissioner General of Rwanda Correctional service showing:
1° identification of the person for whom pardon is applied;
2° offence for which the person for whom pardon is applied was imprisoned;
3° the decision of the court at the last instance that sentenced the person for whom pardon is applied;
4° the period completed in serving the sentence and the remaining period;
5° conduct in prison of the person for whom pardon is applied with supporting evidence;
6° advice of Rwanda Correctional Service on the request of presidential pardon.
