mark :506
original-oid 2ad0d7515142cac436dd0ffaae3e9efbab5e8241
data 442
Article 241: Effects of suspension of penalty
Suspension of penalty does not prevent the payment of court fees and damages. Nor does it extend to the deprivation of rights as a result of conviction. However, deprivation of rights ceases to have effect on the date the offence becomes null and void.
Chapter: CHAPTER II: GROUNDS FOR SUSPENSION OF THE EXECUTION OF A PENALTY AND REMOVAL OF A PENALTY
Section: Section 3: Suspension of a penalty

