original-oid 48b1866ba8af5a7b3230420559f1a25dc891621d
data 249
Article 263: Definition of a dormant company
A company is a dormant company for any period during which no significant accounting transaction occurs.
Chapter: CHAPTER XII: LIMITED LIFE COMPANY AND DORMANT COMPANY
Section: Section 2: Dormant company

blob
mark :817
original-oid 95f294047b7a6b90120f4d2c57da395d4f342426
data 412
Article 264: A company considered to be dormant
A company is deemed to be dormant where it:
1° has been dormant from the time of its formation;
2° has been dormant since the end of its previous accounting period; and is not required to prepare accounts for that period, by a special resolution of shareholders.
Chapter: CHAPTER XII: LIMITED LIFE COMPANY AND DORMANT COMPANY
Section: Section 2: Dormant company

