Article 289: Restoration to register
A company is restored to the register of companies when a notice signed by the Registrar General stating that the company is restored to the register is registered under this Law.
A company that is restored to the register is not deemed to have continued in existence as if it had not been removed from the register.
Chapter: CHAPTER XIV: REGISTRATION, REMOVAL FROM REGISTERS AND INSPECTION OF THE OPERATION OF COMPANIES
Section: Section 2: Removal of a company from the register

